<title>HUNGARY: Hungary BNP-Dresdner reports higher profits for H1.</title>
<headline>Hungary BNP-Dresdner reports higher profits for H1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				  Jan-June 1997     Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		600	 vs	562</p>
<p>    Total assets	     57,952	 vs   46,990</p>
<p>    Adjusted capital	  8,254	 vs     n.a</p>
<p>    Loans to customers     24,769	 vs     n.a.</p>
<p>    Capital adequacy ratio     21.5 pct vs     n.a.</p>
<p>NOTE: BNP-Dresdner Bank (Hungaria) Rt is 50-50 percent owned by Banque Nationale de Paris and Dresdner Bank AG.</p>
<p>The figures are not consolidated and were calculated in accordance with Hungarian Accounting Standards.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
